        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECf_34-2b.lnote.la.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">662</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">p. d. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">p. d. lacking in Hr</seg></note>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude-crib" ana="#fromLatin">After Æthelred his son Edmund reigned almost nine months*, in which he fought manfully five times against Cnut, king of the Danes. But when the last battle was over, they made an agreement between themselves and divided the kingdom of England: half to Cnut and half to Edmund, on this condition, that, if either of them should survive, the other [?] should possess the whole, and that meanwhile neither of them should be crowned. But when this covenant had been confirmed, with all the chief men of England consenting, after the first month Edmund, alas, was taken from this light.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ECf_34-2b.lnote.oe.erkl-clause" n="*" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ebd.</hi> Eadmund II.; Eisenseite; Cnut 2. Über den Vertrag von 1016 <hi rend="italic">s.</hi> zuletzt Larsen <hi rend="italic">Canute</hi> 98. — <hi rend="italic">Post</hi><hi rend="superscript">20</hi> <hi rend="italic">ipsum Aldr. u. E. Ireneside hoc est Latus ferreum, fi.</hi> — <hi rend="italic">et med.</hi> ohne <hi rend="italic">una</hi><hi rend="superscript">34</hi> — <hi rend="italic">messem</hi><hi rend="superscript">10</hi> Rs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Ibid.</hi> Eadmund II.; Eisenseite; Cnut 2. On the treaty of 1016 see most recently Larson <hi rend="italic">Canute</hi> 98. — <hi rend="italic">Post</hi><hi rend="superscript">20</hi> <hi rend="italic">ipsum Aldr. u. E. Ireneside hoc est Latus ferreum, fi.</hi> — <hi rend="italic">et med.</hi> without <hi rend="italic">una</hi><hi rend="superscript">34</hi> — <hi rend="italic">messem</hi><hi rend="superscript">10</hi> Rs</seg></note>
